  "conclusions": [
    "1.524mm cannot bridge the1.77mm gap in the minimum-height, zero-standoff case:0.246mm nominal clearance remains even with maximum battery envelope.",
    "2.032mm gives12.89%-37.5% nominal compression in these limited cases; this does not establish acceptable pressure or reliable contact.",
    "A thinner actual battery increases the gap if bottom seating stays fixed; no minimum battery thickness is established.",
    "55kPa is typical Young modulus, not an allowable cell contact pressure. No force approval inferred.",
    "At2.032mm nominal and-10% thickness, only0.0588mm extra gap remains in the1.77mm case. Unspecified cell thickness and seating variation can consume this margin."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Pad tolerance is sensitivity only; print tolerance, PCB seating, swelling and pad relaxation are omitted.",
    "No permitted cell compressive load established.",
    "Do not reuse1.016mm TDS thermal impedance values for1.524/2.032mm pads.",
    "No assembly geometry adopted; thermal lag, retention and electrical insulation remain unqualified."
